/-!
# Level-N modular functions as fractions over ℂ[j,fᵥ]

Theorem statement: `WLight.exists_levelFraction_of_stable_family`
(`490607a5-50bf-5b84-bea7-42d3fd2f1404`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `786cc53b-f5ea-5b92-be39-5aab5f10fc60`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $N$ be a positive natural number. Fix a family of period pairs $L : \mathbb{H} \to
\mathtt{PeriodPair}$ normalised by $\omega_1(L\tau) = \tau$ and $\omega_2(L\tau) = 1$ for all
$\tau$; a family $W$ indexed by $v \in (\mathbb{Z}/N)^2$ with $W_v(\tau) = (2\pi
i)^{-2}\,\wp_{L\tau}\big((\tilde v_0 \tau + \tilde v_1)/N\big)$, where $\tilde v_i$ denotes the
canonical lift of $v_i$ to $\mathbb{Z}$; a family $\mathtt{fricke}$ with $\mathtt{fricke}_v(\tau) =
-\big(E_4(\tau)E_6(\tau)/\Delta(\tau)\big)/2592 \cdot W_v(\tau)$; and a function $jf$ with $jf(\tau)
= E_4(\tau)^3/\Delta(\tau)$. Let $S$ be a set of functions $\mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ such that
every $G \in S$ is holomorphic (differentiable as a map of complex manifolds), every $G \in S$
satisfies $G \cdot \Delta^m$ bounded at $i\infty$ for some $m \in \mathbb{N}$, $S$ is closed under
precomposition with the action of each $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ on $\mathbb{H}$, and
every $G \in S$ satisfies $G(\gamma\tau) = G(\tau)$ for all $\gamma$ in the principal congruence
subgroup of level $N$ and all $\tau$. Then for every $F \in S$ there exist $a, b : \mathbb{H} \to
\mathbb{C}$, both lying in the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of functions generated by $jf$ together with
the functions $\mathtt{fricke}_v$ for $v \neq 0$, with $b$ not the zero function and $F \cdot b =
a$.

This is the function-level form of the classical statement that every modular function of level $N$
is a rational function of $j$ and the Fricke functions $f_v$: the conclusion is a single fraction
identity $F \cdot b = a$ with numerator and denominator in the polynomial algebra $\mathbb{C}[j, f_v
: v \neq 0]$, no field of fractions being formed, and $b \neq 0$ only as a function (it may vanish
at isolated points). It feeds the rationality statements for $q$-expansion coefficients of forms on
$\Gamma_1(N)$ and the spanning results for Fricke-rational combinations of $E_4$ and $E_6$ powers.

